<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9dd9948e5dad32a51e4681a34404a263a6ea27de" commit="8d29d6608676ed257d4f8925b07809cbe1c232f7" commit_message="[autotest] liststorage: Handling '\040' (space) unicode in mountpoint  In the current scenario, a default case mounts the usb device without logging in and execute file operation. This is not true in a true user scenario.  After login, a non-labelled device is mounted to '/media/removable/USB\ Drive'. When read by python, an octal unicode '\040' replaces ' ' (space) in the above mentioned path. This patch escapes all such octal unicodes.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST= &quot; Tested using 'hardware_UsbBasicFileOperations': Without login - the case passes with no issues as it executes file operations on the device mounted to a default mountpoint. With Login - the case passes as the device is mounted to '/media/removable/USB Drive' and space is handled. &quot; Signed-off-by: pharlapu &lt;puneeth.harlapur@intel.com&gt;  Change-Id: I9dd9948e5dad32a51e4681a34404a263a6ea27de Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/974986 Commit-Ready: Puneeth Harlapur &lt;puneeth.harlapur@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Naresh Solanki &lt;naresh.solanki@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Puneeth Harlapur &lt;puneeth.harlapur@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Naresh Solanki &lt;naresh.solanki@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Bogineni Kasaiah &lt;kasaiahx.bogineni@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Vaishali Paisal &lt;vaishali.paisal@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="974986" owner_email="puneeth.harlapur@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/86/974986/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ib58e9f4e080dd48fbacc7608655fea31e9e333e0" commit="45a6fdb1d2eaf59e421cd97fd3fb565d1bcf87ad" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Move some of the netfilter-related modules to in-kernel  Some of the iptables-restore scripts performed by Android expect some netfilter modules to be already loaded. For instance, the script:    *mangle   -A tetherctrl_mangle_FORWARD -p tcp --tcp-flags SYN SYN \     -j TCPMSS --clamp-mss-to-pmtu   COMMIT  First checks if the &quot;mangle&quot; table is already loaded[1]. If it isn't, it tries to load the &quot;ip6_tables&quot; ko[2] and checks for the table again (since the Android config has all the netfilter modules built-in)[3] without explicitly trying to load the relevant ko (&quot;ip6table_mangle&quot;). This causes the whole operation to fail without attempting to actually run the command (which would have resulted in the kernel loading the kernel by itself).  To avoid the above issue, and to also avoid sprinkling `modprobe` commands all around the system (since Android runs in a container without the CAP_SYS_MODULE capability), this change moves the netfilter-related modules from being as a module to being built in-kernel if they:  * Appear in the android-base.cfg list[4]. * Have the CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_*, CONFIG_IP_NF*, CONFIG_IP6_NF_*   prefixes. * Are not explicitly loaded through other means (which exclude   CONFIG_IP_NF_NAT, CONFIG_IP_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE,   CONFIG_IP6_NF_FILTER).  1: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/iptables/+/master/\ iptables/ip6tables-restore.c#297 2: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/iptables/+/master/\ libxtables/xtables.c#418 3: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/iptables/+/master/\ iptables/ip6tables-restore.c#67 4: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/configs/+/master/\ android-4.4/android-base.cfg  BUG=b:68277526 TEST=The above iptables-restore script now succeeds TEST=third_party/autotest/files/site_utils/bootperf-bin/bootperf      seconds_power_on_to_login:        before: 9.61 (avg, over 10 runs)        after: 9.587 (avg, over 10 runs) Signed-off-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/747003 Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 617f812275dcf2f0d62e42850bf8c4683d991cc6) [drinkcat: renormalized configuration, which changed:  - CONFIG_IP6_NF_TARGET_REJECT from y to m, as IP6_NF_FILTER is    currently set as module  - CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_REDIRECT from m to y, due to    CONFIG_IP_NF_TARGET_REDIRECT=y. ] Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: Ib58e9f4e080dd48fbacc7608655fea31e9e333e0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/991613 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="991613" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/13/991613/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I4d14a281f48af3e68263832dfb092c98ba6ec291" commit="e0b34f1772146ac9edad2f8164bc822455fb70d9" commit_message="CHROMIUM: media: rockchip-vpu: Use OUTPUT resolution for HW programming  The V4L2 Codec API specification, as of today, states that coded resolution of the stream matches the resolution of OUTPUT queue after being adjusted by the driver. However, hardware programming code in rockchip-vpu driver mixes the resolution of CAPTURE queue with the resolution of OUTPUT queue. If the resolution on both queues ends up different, the hardware gets confused and produces invalid stream. Fix it by always using resolution of OUTPUT queue.  While at it, replace some open coded rounded-up division to macroblock size with MB_WIDTH/HEIGHT() macros we had defined for this purpose.  BUG=b:71882314 TEST=run cts -m CtsMediaTestCases  --test android.media.cts.DecodeEditEncodeTest#testVideoEditQCIF  Change-Id: I4d14a281f48af3e68263832dfb092c98ba6ec291 Signed-off-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/992080 Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="992080" owner_email="tfiga@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/80/992080/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I90356a20fa42383f6120611f830c34e1ef5a208e" commit="5cb5b2f61803540da057cb43130219b740549bcc" commit_message="lakitu: drop usgae of --install in docker-runc makefile  The &quot;go build -i&quot; invocation may slightly help with incremental recompilation, but it will cause builds to fail if $GOROOT is not writeable by the current user. For more details, see https://github.com/docker/runc/commit/6581d0f488b3bfa00760cc71c5f1fccfee302b0d  TEST=emerge-lakitu app-emulation/docker-runc BUG=chromium:828187 RELEASE_NOTE=None  Change-Id: I90356a20fa42383f6120611f830c34e1ef5a208e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/994235 Commit-Ready: Ke Wu &lt;mikewu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Ke Wu &lt;mikewu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="994235" owner_email="mikewu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/35/994235/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I26d52fa5f0a3363237b10da83a324584f9b632f9" commit="ac9bb87d9c2db345e115b63e24d45c9a7b630819" commit_message="network_WiFi_BgscanBackoff: Add support for 5GHz  This test currently uses 2.4 GHz channels. Refactor it to make channels configurable. Keep the control file for the current configuration of channels 1 and 11. Add a new control file to test channels on 5 GHz, especially channels 149 and 153 which we care about on certain Intel SoCs.  BUG=chromium:827829 TEST=This is a test, confirm that both control.wifi_bgscan_backoff and control.5760_noise_check pass on my Soraka.  Change-Id: I26d52fa5f0a3363237b10da83a324584f9b632f9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/989395 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="989395" owner_email="kirtika@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/95/989395/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib90cd47e9a2a75615ac7a9ff651106dcffd2057c" commit="effe906f0319a1e8274d5b5e0ead04ca4eeba653" commit_message="bluetooth: Add handler to impersonate ObjectManager  This CL adds an ObjectManagerInterfaceMultiplexer that impersonates the source ObjectManager that it consumes. At this moment this ObjectManagerInterfaceMultiplexer doesn't actually do multiplexing as only 1 source is supported.  Future work will allow multiple sources to be impersonated and the multiplexer needs to resolve clashing objects/interfaces/properties/methods.  This CL is part of go/bluez-split-stack-phase-1 (Work 1).  BUG=chromium:812468 TEST=Added unit test  Change-Id: Ib90cd47e9a2a75615ac7a9ff651106dcffd2057c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/982745 Commit-Ready: Sonny Sasaka &lt;sonnysasaka@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Sonny Sasaka &lt;sonnysasaka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="982745" owner